AB  - Scientific Knowledge Graphs (SKGs) are foundational for automated discovery and reasoning. However, their construction faces critical hurdles due to the heterogeneity of scientific literature, where essential information is fragmented across complex text and unstructured visual modalities like figures and tables. Furthermore, the rapid growth of publications makes continuous updates necessary, as rebuilding from scratch is costly. To address this, we propose MSKGCF, a novel framework for Multimodal Scientific Knowledge Graph Construction and Fusion. MSKGCF adopts a two-stage extraction strategy, first entity recognition, then relation classification, driven by a general-purpose Teacher LLM (GPT-4o) to capture information across text and visual modalities. A fine-tuned multimodal Student LLM (Qwen3VL) is then trained online via an uncertainty-driven active learning loop, which uses model entropy to identify low-confidence samples ("hard" examples) and prioritizes them as in-context references for few-shot learning. Furthermore, we introduce a logic-based fusion mechanism to integrate disparate sub-graphs via LLM-based conflict resolution, ensuring scalability. Experiments show that MSKGCF outperforms existing methods in extraction accuracy. A downstream case study on Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) confirms that the resulting knowledge graph improves scientific question answering.
ER  - 

