AB  - Intelligent Tutoring Systems (ITSs) have proven effective in delivering adaptive and personalized instruction, yet their scalability remains limited by the high cost of authoring and maintaining instructional content. Recent advances in Large Language Models (LLMs) offer new opportunities to enrich ITSs with natural dialogue, dynamic explanations, and personalized feedback. However, challenges such as factual accuracy, reliability, and pedagogical alignment hinder their direct use in education. This paper presents a case study and technical implementation of a successful integration of LLMs within an ITS framework. The proposed architecture combines a recommendation engine with an LLM-powered chatbot, supported by grounding, scaffolding, and verification mechanisms to ensure pedagogical soundness. In this paper, we describe the layered system design, core integration components, and interaction pipeline that enable seamless learner engagement. Our contribution demonstrates how LLMs can complement ITSs in practice, reducing authoring effort, improving adaptability, and enhancing learner interaction through a reliable hybrid approach.
