AB  - Traditional one-shot question-answering paradigms are insufficient for supporting continuous, structured, and interdisciplinary learning in software engineering education. This paper proposes an endless learning framework driven by Model-as-a-Service (MaaS) and Educational Agents, aiming to transform a learner’s query into a sustainable learning process. The framework introduces the Learning Task Package as a core unit, integrating knowledge graphs, evidence retrieval, large language model generation, learning assessment, and adaptive recommendation to support concept explanation, evidence grounding, task generation, feedback, and learning path extension. A prototype system is implemented using Yi-learning as an interdisciplinary case to validate the feasibility of the proposed approach. Classroom comparison experiments and component-level evaluations are designed to assess learning continuity, effectiveness, content reliability, and interdisciplinary value. The results demonstrate that the proposed framework provides a service-oriented paradigm for AI-supported continuous learning and offers practical insights for intelligent education system design.
